From 4e244cc0da8594864ae234846f0baf204c3fc993 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 22:39:13 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 59/65] rpc, validation: report the tripwire outputs
 (gettripwireinfo) and log their spends

gettripwireinfo returns, from one cs_main snapshot of the active chainstate,
the tip it reads the state at (tip_hash, tip_height), the activation height
and the leaf version of the P2MR tripwire rules, each tripwire output with
its state, and ec_disabled_next_block. The state is "unspent" while the
output is an unspent output created below the activation height, and
"missing" otherwise: the UTXO set does not tell a spent output from one that
never existed or was created too late, so the RPC names no spending
transaction. The outputs the code fixes for the Ark-0 signet also carry the
x-only key their leaf checks and a label; an output given by an option has
neither, since an outpoint does not say which key it is locked to. Where the
rules are not enabled the RPC fails.

The node logs, only for the active chainstate and only where the chain has
tripwire outputs:
- at startup, the state of the outputs at the tip and whether elliptic curve
  checks in leaf version 0xe0 fail in the next block;
- when a block reaches the activation height, the same;
- for each input of a block that spends a tripwire output, once ConnectTip
  has connected the block and set the tip: the output, the spending
  transaction, the block, and the height from which elliptic curve checks
  fail, the activation height or the next block, whichever is higher, or
  that they already do. ConnectBlock also checks proposals, candidates that
  turn out invalid and blocks VerifyDB connects again, and the background
  chainstate of an assumeutxo snapshot connects blocks the active chain
  already has, so none of those log a spend.
